# Evidence: prefer kernel-marked USERDEF DRM modes

## Provenance and scope

This is a self-contained extraction of the existing 2026-09-28 DragonBoard
410c cold-control results, not a new hardware run. It accompanies the rebased
landing of pocketboot PR #36. The source is the refs/notes/evidence note on
pocketboot lab commit c90012f51fb90d608bccd1b6772cea4308d6d8e0, also attached to
Linux commit 390b5df1e6a879d9a7c26b3d598a76c902fee99e.

The lab commit, original PR commit 56c9c917911179961fa9c323b7511b0d7d8ffc7e,
and landing commit 39913782fc68cd8506f853649da2f72f41dfc02a have the same stable
patch-id: 8bd866ed2307df2b9a214f5ee372fe6bd2d9d6e2. The landing commit changes
only the USERDEF > PREFERRED > pixel-area mode-ranking key; it does not parse
video=, change connector selection, change equal-key ordering, or add a
modeset retry. Its complete rebased build has not been re-tested by this note.

## Test setup

Board: DragonBoard 410c (APQ8016/MSM8916), ADV7533 HDMI, no attached HDMI sink
or capture dongle. Modes were forced by video=HDMI-A-1:<mode>e.

Pocketboot initramfs: lab commit c90012f51fb90d608bccd1b6772cea4308d6d8e0,
with the PR #23 HDMI configuration and PR #24 fixed secure-page-table work
below the UI change, not plain main. Initramfs SHA-256:
50fb48314e9a2ccb5a1b5023622ab4917292f08ad0cb70a90ad4a8dab890e307.

Kernel: pocketboot/msm8916 base d87323486b79a31b9b25eb6fe30f1b503f142ff2
(Linux 7.1.0-rc6+) with the BASE lab patch set documented in the full note.
The three cold controls used that same BASE kernel, without a kexec hop.

## Cold-control observations

| Control | Requested mode | Observed dri/0/state CRTC mode | Buffers | Result |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| C1-cold-1280x720 | 1280x720@60e | "1280x720": 60 74440 ... 0x20 0x6; USERDEF CVT, active=1 | 3 x 3686400 bytes | Requested geometry active |
| C2-cold-640x480 | 640x480@60e | "640x480": 60 25175 ... 0x60 0xa; DRIVER|USERDEF, active=1 | 3 x 1228800 bytes | Requested smaller geometry active |
| C5-cold-1920x1080 | 1920x1080@30e | "1280x720": 60 74250 ... 0x40 0x5; DRIVER only | 3 x 3686400 bytes | Requested mode rejected by kernel; driver fallback selected |

For C5, cold-dmesg.txt line 282 recorded:

    msm_mdp 1a01000.display-controller: [drm] User-defined mode not supported: "1920x1080": 30 80192 ...

The kernel rejected the 80.192 MHz CVT mode at mode_valid. This is not evidence
that pocketboot can honor a mode removed by kernel validation.

## Caveats

- The old-code selection of 1024x768 instead of a requested 640x480 was derived
  from code, not reproduced as a before/after hardware comparison.
- These observations establish programmed CRTC state and allocation, not
  visual output: no sink or capture dongle was connected.
- Mode type varied across later lab rows (the original note's A2 caveat):
  1280x720 was sometimes USERDEF CVT at 74440 kHz and sometimes DRIVER|USERDEF
  CEA at 74250 kHz, while C5 used DRIVER only. ADV7533 sink sensing fluctuated;
  geometry and GEM allocation stayed the same.
- INFO-level pocketboot UI/page-flip messages were absent because kmsg tracing
  defaulted to WARN. The observations came from dri/0/state and dri/0/gem.
- Each cold control had one baseline MDP5 modeset underrun and no cb=4 faults.
- This note does not establish behavior with EDID, on fixed DSI panels, or
  under multi-connector configurations.

